synopsis:
  Store annotations more compactly in interface files
description:
  Values serialized with ``GHC.Serialized.serializeWithData`` (the payload
  of ``ANN`` pragmas) now encode numbers with LEB128 and fold the constructor
  index into the constructor tag, instead of the fixed-width encoding of
  ``Data.Binary``. Most constructors now take one byte, and small numbers two.
  For example, ``[1..100] :: [Int]`` goes from 1509 bytes to 338 and
  ``Just True`` from 18 bytes to 2.
